  "body": "Smaller release binaries:\n\n- **Documented install command now strips debug symbols** (`-ldflags=\"-s -w\"`), shrinking the installed binary by roughly a third (~9.9MB → ~6.6MB on macOS arm64). This only applies to what you actually run, since `go install` always builds from source on your machine — see the README for the updated command (both the CLI/TUI and `-tags gui` variants).\n- Added `make dist` for maintainers: cross-builds stripped, versioned CLI/TUI binaries for darwin/linux amd64+arm64, for anyone who'd rather download a prebuilt binary than build from source.\n\nNo functional/CLI changes since v0.6.1."
